---
import SectionTitle from "../layouts/SectionTitle.astro";
import PortfolioNav from "../layouts/PortfolioNav.astro";
import VideoScript from "../layouts/VideoScript.astro";
import Video from "../layouts/Video.astro";
import Image from "../layouts/Image.astro";
import Footer from "../layouts/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../layouts/Header.astro"

---

<html lang="en">
    <Header title="Hint System"/>
    <body class="hint bg-[#F2E8D5] min-h-screen text-[#302C32]">
        <PortfolioNav />
        <SectionTitle
            title="Hint System"
            imgsrc="/portfolio/hintsystem.png"
            titlecolor="text-[#7A1F3D]"
        />
        <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 space-y-3 mb-6">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>
                I developed a clue system for puzzle/mystery games, implemented
                in a test scene based on the tutorial for the board game series
                Unlock! (Demaegd, C., 2017) to demonstrate my ability, as a
                systems programmer, to produce a feature that can be easily
                reused in other projects of this game genre. This system aim to
                adapt assistance to player preferences.
            </p>
            <p>
                This development is based on accessibility (tailoring help to
                players' needs), reusability (being able to integrate this
                system easily into any puzzle/mystery game) and
                non-intrusiveness (guiding the player towards clues without
                interrupting their experience).
            </p>

            <h2>Used Tools</h2>
            <p>I used Unreal Engine 5.6 in blueprint to create this system.</p>

            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <p>The system follows several steps.</p>
            <p>First, a timer is started.</p>
            <p>
                Once the timer has run out, the attached transmitter searches
                for receivers attached to the objects involved in solving the
                puzzles.
            </p>
            <p>For a receiver to be valid, it must:</p>
            <ul class="list">
                <li>Be within a limited area around the player</li>
                <li>
                    Contain clues with the same progression ID as the player
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                If several objects are valid, the one closest to the player is
                selected.
            </p>
            <p>
                Once the object has been identified, the transmitter instructs
                it to play a dialogue corresponding to the current progress
                identifier.
            </p>
            <p>
                When the player completes a step in solving a puzzle, the
                progression ID is incremented.
            </p>
            <h2>Accessibility</h2>
            <p>
                Rather than finding a one-size-fits-all solution for every type
                of player, I decided instead to create accessibility options.
            </p>
            <Image imgsrc="/portfolio/accessibility.png" />

            <h3>Frequency</h3>
            <p>
                The player can choose to increase or decrease the frequency with
                which clues appear.
            </p>
            <h3>Display</h3>
            <p>The player can also choose between three display modes:</p>
            <ul class="list">
                <li>
                    <span class="bold">No hints</span>: The player will receive no hint notifications.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="bold">Legacy Mode</span>: The player will receive a hint every time the
                    timer runs out.
                    <Video videosrc="/portfolio/legacymode.mp4" />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class=bold>Dynamic Mode:</span> The player will receive a notification every
                    time the timer runs out and can decide whether to
                    display the hint.
                    <Video videosrc="/portfolio/dynamicmode.mp4" />
                </li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Links</h2>
            <p>
                <span class="bold">Project repository</span>: <a
                    href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1px251h8yfgN-Uq6tA-qv9JQ9zmdAaQyl/view?usp=sharing"
                    >https://drive.google.com/file/d/1px251h8yfgN-Uq6tA-qv9JQ9zmdAaQyl/view?usp=sharing</a
                >
            </p>
            <h2>Inspirations</h2>
            <p>Demaegd, C. (2017). Unlock ! [Board Game]. Space Cowboys.</p>
